---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';

const days = (await getCollection('gamedays')).sort(
  (a, b) => b.data.date.valueOf() - a.data.date.valueOf()
);
const next = days.find(d => d.data.status !== 'past') ?? days[0];
---
<Base
  title="New here"
  description="What actually happens at a Dice & Tale game day in Berlin, hour by hour, for people who have never played a tabletop roleplaying game."
>
  <section class="head">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Never played before</p>
      <h1>What actually happens</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Written for the person who has been meaning to try this for two years and
        keeps not coming because they don't know what they'd be walking into.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="strip bleed">
    <Photo slug="gm-with-the-dice-bag" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 50vw" ratio="3/2" />
    <Photo slug="four-and-a-round-table" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 50vw" ratio="3/2" />
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <span class="s-when mono">Before</span>
          <div>
            <h2>You book one table, not the day</h2>
            <p>
              The schedule lists every table, who is running it, what system, how
              long, and how many seats are left. Pick one that says beginner
              friendly. You are booking a seat at that specific table, for those
              specific hours — not committing to eleven hours in a basement.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="s-when mono">Arriving</span>
          <div>
            <h2>You turn up ten minutes early and write your name on a sticker</h2>
            <p>
              Someone is on the door. They tell you which table is yours and point
              at it. Nearly everybody arrives alone; the name badges exist because
              nobody knows each other yet either.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="s-when mono">First 20 min</span>
          <div>
            <h2>The game master hands you a character</h2>
            <p>
              On a beginner table the characters already exist — a page each, with
              the numbers filled in. You read yours, pick which one you like, and
              the game master explains the rules you need for the next hour. Not
              the whole rulebook. The next hour.
            </p>
            <p>
              This is also when the table agrees what it does not want in the story:
              the <a href="/code-of-conduct">lines and veils</a> conversation. It
              takes about three minutes and it is normal.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="s-when mono">The next 3&ndash;4h</span>
          <div>
            <h2>Someone describes a situation and you say what you do</h2>
            <p>
              That is the whole game. The game master describes where you are, you
              say what your character tries, and when the outcome is uncertain you
              roll a die to find out. There is no script, no winning, and no way to
              be bad at it. Nobody at the table has read anything you haven't.
            </p>
            <p>
              If a scene goes somewhere you would rather it didn't, you say so and
              it stops. No reason needed, no one asks for one.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="s-when mono">After</span>
          <div>
            <h2>You leave, or you stay for another one</h2>
            <p>
              Tables run in three blocks through the day. Plenty of people play one
              and go home. Plenty stay until the last table finishes and end up in
              the group chat.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bring">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <div class="cols">
        <div>
          <h2>Bring</h2>
          <ul class="tick">
            <li>Yourself</li>
            <li>Something to drink</li>
            <li>Ten minutes of slack in your schedule</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2>Don't need</h2>
          <ul class="cross">
            <li>Dice</li>
            <li>A character</li>
            <li>A rulebook, or to have read one</li>
            <li>A group, or a single person you know</li>
            <li>Any experience whatsoever</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="qs">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <h2>The questions people actually ask</h2>
      <dl>
        <dt>Is it all Dungeons &amp; Dragons?</dt>
        <dd>
          No. Recent tables have run Call of Cthulhu, Mothership, Brindlewood Bay,
          Savage Worlds, Fate, the Witcher game and Blood on the Clocktower. D&amp;D
          is one of many.
        </dd>

        <dt>I'm not a performer. Do I have to do voices?</dt>
        <dd>
          No. Most people at most tables say "I try to talk him out of it" rather
          than acting it. Both are fine and they sit at the same table.
        </dd>

        <dt>What if I'm the only person there on my own?</dt>
        <dd>
          You won't be. Most tables are five strangers, which is why the game master
          spends the first twenty minutes making that not matter.
        </dd>

        <dt>My German isn't good.</dt>
        <dd>
          Most tables run in English. One recent table ran deliberately in bad German
          as the entire premise. Berlin is like that.
        </dd>

        <dt>What does it cost?</dt>
        <dd>{next.data.entry}</dd>

        <dt>What if I book and then can't come?</dt>
        <dd>
          Cancel your seat so a person on the waiting list gets it. Tables fill and
          somebody is always waiting. That is the only etiquette rule we ask for.
        </dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <h2>Next one is {next.data.date.toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long' })}</h2>
      <p>{next.data.venue}, {next.data.address}. {next.data.startTime}&ndash;{next.data.endTime}.</p>
      <p class="cta-btns">
        <a class="btn" href={`/game-days/${next.id}`}>See the tables</a>
        <a class="btn btn--quiet" href="/join">Get the next date by email</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .head { padding-bottom: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.4rem); }
  .strip {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 3px;
    background: var(--rule); border-block: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .steps { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .steps > li {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 7rem 1fr; gap: 0 1.6rem;
    padding: 1.8rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .steps > li:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .s-when {
    font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold); padding-top: 0.5rem; border-top: 2px solid var(--gold);
    align-self: start;
  }
  .steps h2 { font-size: 1.16rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }

  .bring { background: var(--paper-2); border-block: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .cols { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2.5rem; }
  .cols h2 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
  .tick, .cross { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .tick li, .cross li {
    padding: 0.4rem 0 0.4rem 1.6rem; position: relative; font-size: 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .tick li::before { content: "+"; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--gold); font-weight: 600; }
  .cross li::before { content: "\2013"; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--ink-mute); }

  .qs dl { margin: 1.5rem 0 0; }
  .qs dt {
    font-family: "Cinzel", Georgia, serif; font-size: 1.02rem;
    margin: 1.6rem 0 0.4rem; color: var(--ink);
  }
  .qs dd { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 64ch; }

  .cta { background: var(--paper-2); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .cta-btns { display: flex; gap: 0.8rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1.4rem; }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .steps > li { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.7rem; }
    .s-when { border-top: 0; padding-top: 0; }
    .cols { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.8rem; }
    .strip { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
